sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-task-vm-destroy.yaml (+ the shared task-vm-destroy child, provider-power for UpCloud, model-revoke and operation-node-remove children), docs/reference/compute-drivers.md, docs/reference/task-vm-native-provision.md, docs/reference/tasks.md, DECISIONS R1-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02 (second pass), rules 22 (one command is one exec argv: the VM delete and the seed volume delete are two argvs, so two steps; no TypeScript plan, seed decode or terminal fold), 9 (one read-back of the VM and the volume, one native `assert`), 14 (no `result` step in the child or the root; the Gateway reads the run's step statuses and builds the receipt from its captured intent), 16 (no read before the forced delete; an absent VM or volume counts as done and the end check proves it), 21 (the child stays: tasks.cancel and failed provisions run it too, so it is a typed boundary).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · nothing admits it now
  %% kind: task_vm.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane DC icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant DC as Destroy child<br/>task-vm-destroy
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Node 13 over ssh
  participant HUB as VPN hub<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>task VM 333 · task #5181 · Node 13
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - the `DestroyTaskVm` job, when group 77 completes or is cancelled, or its workspace is removed
  %%> - nothing now: the host sweep no longer admits a `destroying` VM, and a group end releases its task VM with `task_vm.slot_release` (docs/cli/tasks/vm-release.mmd); this kind goes with the old provision
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no other task holds `task_vm:333`; a repeated admission returns the same open task
  %%> - no workspace, Route, protected Node resource or unpublished approved work remains on guest Node 340
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task VM 333 is `destroying`; guest Node 340 is `removing`
  %%> - task #5181 records the provider input, whether a model key exists, the seed volume name and the Node removal intent
  %%> - vault copies for the model key, the router keys and, for UpCloud, the API token
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-destroy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the intent and `execution_secrets` as vault key names; no decode step reads them (rule 15)
  SW->>DC: Destroy the task VM<br/>workflow · task-vm-destroy
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the root's one step runs the shared child; its steps follow on its own lane
  %%> Why a child:
  %%> - tasks.cancel and a failed provision run the same child, so it is a typed boundary
  DC->>DC: Revoke the model key<br/>model · task-vm-model-revoke
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes VM 333's model key from the model router from 209 and confirms the anchor key stays
  %%> - two Ansible phases on 209, `anchor` and `revoke`: HTTPS calls to the router, no script
  %%> When:
  %%> - a `guard` skips it when VM 333 has no model key
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - the provider delete waits for it, so a deleted VM never leaves a live key
  %%> Held open:
  %%> - one 209 script until an official HTTP behavior covers the router API
  alt Incus host
    DC->>H: Delete the VM<br/>ssh exec · incus delete --force
    %%> How:
    %%> - one pinned `@swamp/ssh exec` argv: `sudo timeout 180 incus delete --force --project orbit-tasks -- tvm-333`, running or stopped
    %%> - an absent VM counts as done; the end check proves it is gone
    %%> Cancel:
    %%> - after this step succeeds, the task can no longer be cancelled
    DC->>H: Delete the seed volume<br/>ssh exec · incus volume delete
    %%> How:
    %%> - `sudo timeout 180 incus storage volume delete --project orbit-tasks -- <pool> tvm-333-topology-seed`, after the VM releases it
    %%> - an absent volume counts as done
  else UpCloud overflow
    DC->>DC: Read the server<br/>inspect · task-vm-provider-power
    DC->>DC: Stop the server<br/>stop · task-vm-provider-power
    %%> When:
    %%> - a `guard` skips it when the server is not running
    DC->>DC: Delete the server<br/>delete · task-vm-provider-power
    %%> How:
    %%> - each is one inline `curl` on 209 with the token through `--variable`; the delete removes the server with its storage, and its own read-back proves it gone
  end
  DC->>DC: Forget the guest host key<br/>vm-known-hosts · 209 known_hosts
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the guest address from the 209 worker's `known_hosts`, so the next VM there brings its own key
  %%> Why:
  %%> - mirrors `Pin the guest host key` in provision (rule 17)
  %%> When:
  %%> - a `guard` skips it when the VM had no WireGuard address
  %%> - runs in parallel with the Node removal
  DC->>HUB: Remove the guest Node<br/>cleanup · operation-node-remove
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - canonical Node removal of Node 340 under this run: removes its hub peer file and reloads the peer set
  %%> - no guest probe or SSH to the deleted VM
  %%> When:
  %%> - a `guard` skips it when Node 340 is already gone
  opt Incus host
    DC->>H: Read the host again<br/>ssh exec · forEach of 2
    %%> How:
    %%> - two parallel argvs: `incus query /1.0/instances?project=orbit-tasks` and the custom volumes of the pool
    DC->>DC: Check the VM is gone<br/>assert
    %%> End check:
    %%> - a native `assert`: neither `tvm-333` nor `tvm-333-topology-seed` is listed
  end
  alt every step passes
    DC-->>SW: Child succeeded<br/>tvm-333 gone
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>tvm-333 destroyed
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run once; it builds the cleanup receipt from the captured intent
    %%> Result:
    %%> - removes Node 340 and its Process records, marks task VM 333 `destroyed` and clears its Pi token
    %%> - task #5181 succeeds; the host slot is free for the next claim
  else a step fails
    H--xDC: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    %%> When:
    %%> - the revoke, a delete, the Node removal or the end check fails
    DC--xSW: Child failed<br/>failed step
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>destroy_failed, failed step
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5181 fails; task VM 333 stays `destroying` with the error and keeps its credentials and cleanup intent
    %%> - Node 340 becomes `failed` with `failed_step` `remove:operation`
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - nothing admits the VM again; the release of the group's task VM replaces this path
  end
